                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I never got far in this one as a child because it was merely one of the dozens of games on a shareware compilation CD. There both is and isn't a surprising amount of content in the first/free episode. On one hand, playing through it blind is a handful of puzzles, some mild top-down combat, and running around talking to NPCs. I dare to call it somewhat modern in that there are no lives, you simply start over on each screen when you die. On the other hand, the speedrun for this episode is less than 12 minutes once you know in which order to tackle the screens.\n\nIt didn't really click with me as an adult, but if you're somehow reading this review I recommend checking it out to see how PC gaming used to be.",
